<h1>EBWiki Guidelines for Adding Content</h1>
<h2>Volunteer Editors</h2>
<p>Our goal is to gather comprehensive and accurate data on cases of overreach and abuse by law enforcement against people of color. Anyone with web access can edit or create cases. When editors disagree, they work together toward a page that fairly represents the current facts, evidenced by external sources.</p>
<h2>Adding content</h2>
<p>See the <a href="/instructions">instructions</a> for adding and editing cases and agencies. Read more on <a href="/about">our mission</a>.</p>
<h2>History and follow</h2>
<p>The history page shows who changed a case and why. Follow (still on Rails until identity moves) emails you when a case you track is updated. Poor-quality edits can be reversed because every change is recorded.</p>
<h2>Intellectual Property</h2>
<p>Contributions remain the property of their creators, while the CC-BY-SA and GFDL licenses ensure the content is freely distributable and reproducible.</p>
